# The live values for this shop's Supabase project.
#
# Normally this file would carry placeholders and .env.local the real values.
# Here it carries the real ones deliberately, so a fresh clone runs with no
# setup at all — copy it to .env.local and the app works.
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_, meaning Next.js inlines them into the browser bundle
# at build time. Every phone that loads the app already has them, so they
# identify the project rather than protecting it. Row Level Security is what
# actually protects the data, which is why the schema tests assert isolation
# between shops rather than trusting the key.
#
# Two consequences worth knowing:
#   * A rotated key needs a REBUILD, not a restart — the old one is baked into
#     the last bundle.
#   * If this repository is ever made public, rotate the anon key in Supabase
#     (Settings -> API) and put placeholders back here.
#
# The service_role key must never appear in this file or anywhere else in the
# repository. That one bypasses RLS completely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xlbcxgfdzfwheccsluat.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InhsYmN4Z2ZkemZ3aGVjY3NsdWF0Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NzYyMzUyNTcsImV4cCI6MjA5MTgxMTI1N30.C8zJC23-O-xp_FbUgeaxyUjiyat7XvZP4pJPcEQgbeU
